<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrés de Urdaneta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1508–1568</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrés de Urdaneta was a Spanish navigator and Augustinian friar. Sailing with the expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel López de Legazpi</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1565, he found the return route across the Pacific to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> by sailing north to catch the westerly winds, a route known as the tornaviaje. It made possible the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila-galleon">Manila galleon</a> trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> for 250 years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andres-de-urdaneta.jpg" alt="Andrés de Urdaneta" width="213" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andres_de_Urdaneta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
